nd expert ratings.", "Incumbent Nick LaLota (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Nick LaLota, a first-term Republican incumbent, seeks re-election in a Long Island district that leans Republican by about four points. He holds a large financial advantage, having raised $4.4 million to Chris Gallant's $1.6 million, though Gallant's totals rose after a viral story about old promotional photos drew national attention. Most expert ratings place the race in the Likely Republican column, with two outlets calling it Solid Republican and others Lean Republican.\n\nThe only public poll, a Democratic-sponsored survey from December 2025, showed LaLota ahead by three points, well within uncertainty. Prediction markets price his re-election chances near 85 percent. The race likely hinges on whether the national environment and Gallant's fundraising surge make the contest genuinely competitive in the final weeks, or whether the incumbent's established profile and the district's lean hold. A Republican win by a moderate margin is the expected outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1953, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.158, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1553, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.188, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1399, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0851, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1487, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1542, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1035, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1186, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1205, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.124, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1216, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1197, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.084, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1405, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem"